WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.720
[Disclaimer: Characters, locations,
and all depicted events are fictional

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.470
and for entertainment purposes only;
viewer discretion is advised]

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:17.460
[Your Third Series]

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.340
Your limbs are all hurt.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.730
How can you go back to living alone?

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:21.770
You're staying with me.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.840
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.640
I'm Thee,

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.240
a caretaker here.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.400
Please take care of me and guide me.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.040
You two are close?

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.800
And I cannot be?

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.440
It has been a while since I met Mr. Sarm.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.730
All he has been leaving me
every day is a lunchbox

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.840
hanging on the fence in the morning.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.140
He must have been so busy

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.840
that he had little to no time...

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.280
Getting to see
the roof of your house is enough.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.040
Anything I can help you with, Mr. Sarm?

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.230
Oh, Little Jam.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.829
It's been so long,

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.130
and that's how you say hi?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.840
And...is there anything you need?

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:57.840
Oh...

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.530
Do I need to have

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.340
something on my mind
to come see you?

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.150
Not exactly.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.460
I am just confused

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.910
about why you are here.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:12.930
I'm here to ask you

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:14.650
if the grilled squid

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.670
was tasty at all.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.550
The grilled squid.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.740
Oh,

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.850
the grilled squid from the green market.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.940
It was pretty good.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:29.510
Hot

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:30.190
and tasty.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:30.950
Of course.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.610
You've given your heart to grilled squid.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:33.970
Didn't you say
boiled crabs were the best?

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.270
Weren't they your favorite?

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.230
The crabs are upset, you know?

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.040
Who says I've lost my heart to that?

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:43.940
For me,

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.250
boiled crabs are number one.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.140
Hey.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:56.240
Hm?

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.940
Are you close with Thee now?

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.520
Why do you hang out with him so much?

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.960
Well, I have been working with Thee lately.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:04.870
Just "Thee"?

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:05.640
Mm.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:06.600
Thee.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:07.420
Of course,

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.460
you call everybody else by their names.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.600
Thee,

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:11.510
Song,

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:12.400
and "Wasin."

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:14.960
When will you call me by my name?

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:16.649
When are you going to call me "Sarm"?

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:17.700
The next business day?

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:18.440
Two business days?

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:19.410
Or three business days?

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:22.570
It's okay, Little Jam.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:23.510
It's fine.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:24.650
It's getting late;

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.040
go and get some rest.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:27.750
I'm going home.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:29.870
It's time to leave.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:30.670
Huh?

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.040
Mr. Sarm.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:35.350
Mr. Sarm again.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:36.690
What is it?

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.230
Have a safe trip home.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:42.570
Mm.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.350
- Ow!
- Oh!

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:47.270
Mr. Sarm!

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:48.400
What is it?

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.240
Are you alright?

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.120
I fell into the trap you made.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.560
What trap?

00:04:58.770 --> 00:04:59.840
Love trap.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.300
- Ow!
- Hey!

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.550
- Hey...
- I'm caught in your love trap.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:08.820
See?

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:10.410
Oh.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.670
This kind of love trap.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:12.440
You feel me?

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:13.910
- Ow...
- Hey!

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.520
Are you sure you are alright?

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.220
I am...alright, of course.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:27.890
[Your Third Series]

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:42.020
♫Still feeling lonely? Well, you've got me,♫

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:46.500
♫Keeping you busy every day♫

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:51.159
♫I might not be the one you wanted,♫

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:55.920
♫But give it time, you'll love me anyway♫

00:05:56.370 --> 00:06:00.900
♫It's your heart, so it's your choice,♫

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:05.360
♫I won't ever stand in your way♫

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:09.750
♫But when they make you blue,♫

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:13.510
♫Can you please let me take care of you?♫

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:19.150
♫I'm here to love you as myself, not as a surrogate♫

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:22.940
♫Let me be your safe space when you need a break♫

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:27.960
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:32.510
♫At least being your third still counts♫

00:06:32.909 --> 00:06:37.460
♫I'm here to love you, no matter who left you with heartache♫

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:41.170
♫Just let me heal your heart, lending you my aid♫

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:46.310
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.320
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:51.550
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.520
[Your Third Series]

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.300
You are here to drink coffee, Thee?

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:15.040
That's right.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:17.170
It's got such a great vibe
in the morning here.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.560
That's why I want to drink coffee here.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.210
Care for a cup of coffee, Jam?

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.340
It's on me.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.970
I am worried that
I will be late for work this afternoon.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.420
What's there to be afraid of?

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:28.840
You're here with me, you see.

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:31.820
No one would dare say anything,

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:33.900
would they?

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:36.040
Right...

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:38.950
Do you get uncomfortable around me?

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:40.630
Not really.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:44.010
You are kind and easygoing.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:45.830
It doesn't feel awkward at all?

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:48.930
Why does it have to be?

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:51.900
Usually,

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.130
people are too scared to approach me.

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:56.820
So it all feels awkward to them.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:58.460
But you...

00:07:58.490 --> 00:07:59.810
Consider yourself lucky

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:01.740
because I gave you
a chance to be here with me.

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:05.630
Right.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.830
Mr. Thee sure is easygoing.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.150
But sometimes, he pushes people...

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.450
and throws his weight around.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.020
Allow me to ask you something.

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.430
As an outsider,

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:20.450
what do you think of Adisuan Farm?

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.730
Adisuan Farm began with an orange farm.

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:27.740
Then, it branched out
into several businesses,

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:29.010
such as dining,

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:29.800
tourism,

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:30.290
and hospitality.

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.320
It is a true one-stop tourism empire

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.740
that is likely to keep growing

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.600
steadily.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.130
Do you know that it's all because of me?

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:43.150
Without me,

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.940
Adisuan Farm wouldn't have grown,

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.240
and there would only be
Uncle Decha's orange farm.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.330
And Mr. Sarm...

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.030
Oh, Sarm?

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.820
He's just a son of Uncle Decha's mistress.

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:58.650
I'm the real deal.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:00.880
Know this.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.430
I'm in the same league as Sib, alright?

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:05.210
When Sib has a problem,

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.180
he always comes straight to me.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.650
You truly are talented, Thee.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:10.730
Well, you know?

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.730
By the way...

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.030
Do you want to be part of this empire?

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:27.920
If you have time, come to my place.

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:31.130
I'll show you my priceless achievements.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:32.790
I keep a lot of

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.610
important things in my office.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.310
Feel free to swing by.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.130
Who do you live with, Thee?

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:44.040
I live alone, actually.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:00.420
This is Jiranat speaking.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:02.750
And this is Traiphop speaking.

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:06.930
Is there anything you need, Mr. Sarm?

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:08.340
I've got everything I need,

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:09.810
except your heart.

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.410
Did you have dinner?

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:15.850
Tell me if you're worried about me.

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:17.330
And tell me if you have feelings for me.

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.640
Are you heading to bed?

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:21.730
Soon, actually.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.210
Please don't.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:24.550
Stay with me for a bit first.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:26.530
I'm driving alone, you know?

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:27.640
And I'm scared of ghosts.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:30.220
Just say hi to them.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.400
They are your friends after all.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:33.420
Oh...

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.040
You and your words.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:37.320
What did you have for dinner?

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:40.740
Instant noodles.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:43.320
A crazy day
wrapped around instant noodles.

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:44.530
Have less of that.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.230
Eat some good food.

00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:48.230
But they are tasty,

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:50.250
and I enjoy having them.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:52.320
I enjoy having you, too.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.730
Then why did you scold me over that?

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.530
Don't confess to anyone yet, okay?

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:10.740
I'm trying to win you over.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:15.230
Talking to Mr. Sarm always feels like...

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:16.730
riding a roller coaster,

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.020
He teases me one second,

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:20.720
sulks the next,

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.320
and then makes me feel things.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:26.840
Have a safe trip home.

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:30.650
Goodnight.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.240
Right.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:38.250
♫I only wish you nothing but the best♫

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:42.580
♫Hoping your smile will never fade♫

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:47.690
♫That's all, for I don't wish
to take someone's place♫

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:57.770
Actually...

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:01.930
I no longer see Mr. Sarm as an immature guy.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:03.390
Perhaps...

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.920
I actually like him,

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.320
but I do not know

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:10.300
how I feel about him exactly.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:13.300
The more this keeps dragging on,

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:14.920
the more confusing it gets.

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:17.220
I have to get this mission over with

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:19.030
so that I can move on.

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:24.730
Tonight...

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:27.630
I am going to snoop around
Mr. Thee's place first.

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:29.440
When the time is right,

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:31.520
I will go there for real.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:21.360
Ow...

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:22.730
Little Jam, are you hurt?

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:23.670
Are you alright...?

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:24.710
The question is for you.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.140
Is your hand hurt?

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.140
I'm fine.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.440
Why are you trying to be so inconspicuous?

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.240
You've got both a taser

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:35.850
and a flashlight.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:38.740
It's like you're about to have a fight.

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:43.730
That sounds ridiculous.

00:13:45.730 --> 00:13:47.000
So where are you going,

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:48.730
hm?

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:52.230
I got hungry,

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:53.620
so I wanted to
get something to eat.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:54.420
Oh.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:55.950
But I got lost,

00:13:57.890 --> 00:13:59.010
and I am starving.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:09.830
Hello.

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:12.720
Aunt Salee, please treat
some wounds at my place.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:13.410
And...

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:14.740
Please prepare dishes for two.

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:16.220
Right.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:20.410
I am not going with you.

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:22.730
Fine.

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:24.440
You want to stay here?

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:25.830
Know this.

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:26.660
This area

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:28.340
is infested with water ghosts.

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:30.040
The orange tree spirits are just as scary.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.320
If you stay here,

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:33.830
they'll take your life!

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:35.130
If your neck gets snapped in half,

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:36.440
don't say I didn't warn you.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.330
No need to scare me.

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:44.620
Be honest.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:47.130
Are you sure you actually lost?

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:49.230
Mm.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:52.730
Are you certain

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:54.740
that you're not plotting anything?

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.030
I am doing nothing.

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:04.830
I'll give you one more chance.

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:06.350
Spit it out.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.120
I said I wasn't plotting anything.

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:15.430
Okay.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:17.430
But if I catch you lying,

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:18.940
even if it's you,

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.250
I won't let it slide.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.130
Why?

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:29.130
If I really am hiding something from you...

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.830
That was just a hypothetical situation

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:34.330
and nothing else.

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:36.610
I'd be furious.

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.250
I'd be mad at you
for a whole week.

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:53.820
Playing cute?

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:54.740
Wait.

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:56.140
Why?

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.010
What do you want?

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:06.940
You can be mad at me for a week if you want,

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:11.540
but you have to forgive me after that, okay?

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:16.610
Wait...

00:16:17.070 --> 00:16:17.820
Hold on.

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:18.730
You...

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:20.920
Hey.

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:23.730
What's wrong?

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:25.620
Isn't this just a hypothetical scenario?

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:26.770
Why are you so emotional?

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:32.840
Come.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.330
Let's leave.

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:52.450
This is nothing at all, Mr. Sarm.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:54.430
It's nothing, Mr. Jam.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:59.040
Allow me to call it a night, then.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:16:59.840
Thank you.

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.220
Goodnight, Aunt.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.020
Thank you.

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:03.330
Goodnight.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.829
I told you I was fine.

00:17:12.099 --> 00:17:13.089
You were being dramatic.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:14.240
What do you mean?

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:14.829
Listen.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.400
Isn't it better to know you're fine

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:17.730
than leave it untreated?

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:20.550
How did you end up there anyway?

00:17:20.569 --> 00:17:22.339
I was at the mayor's child's wedding,

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:24.230
and I was passing by that area.

00:17:25.329 --> 00:17:26.720
That's why I spotted

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:27.839
someone

00:17:27.869 --> 00:17:29.210
acting all inconspicuous.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.630
I almost shot you
right there and then.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:35.250
What were you doing
around my quarters this late?

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.810
Why did you not return to your place?

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:41.150
Oh.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.930
I was patrolling.

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:45.220
The farm is vast, you see.

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:47.650
What would happen if a thief sneaked in?

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:49.600
Thus, we need to do
a bit of patrolling, correct?

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.290
It's close to New Year.

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:55.750
Do you have plans for your costume?

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.650
I actually have nothing in mind.

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:00.930
If you don't,

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:01.640
then

00:18:02.340 --> 00:18:03.630
how about we wear matching costumes?

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:07.040
Like what?

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.610
Bananas in Pyjamas.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.330
You'll dress as B1,

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.510
and I'll dress as B2.

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:18.330
Let's dress up as a pair.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:22.740
B1 and B2.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.240
But the theme is something spooky.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.110
Spooky.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:31.830
Mm.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.080
Ghost bananas.

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:37.840
Huh?

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:40.050
That wouldn't fly, would it?

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.050
If that's the case,

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:43.780
how about

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:45.910
we exchange gifts?

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:50.240
Do you mean

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:52.570
doing a lucky draw?

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.050
Not that.

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:55.230
Like,

00:18:55.470 --> 00:18:57.240
you and me,

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.230
Jam and Sarm.

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:01.750
Just the two of us.

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:13.440
Mm.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:15.920
Alright.

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:17.020
Lovely.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:40.530
Jam.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:41.210
Hm?

00:19:41.230 --> 00:19:43.010
Why does this feel so spooky?

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.050
There is nothing to be afraid of.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:47.030
Who exactly

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:49.530
voted for this theme?

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:51.420
- Boo!
- Whoa!

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:54.240
Doctor Ning-nong!

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:55.930
You scared us.

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:57.570
What ghosts
are you dressing up as?

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.550
I am dressing up as a krahang.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:03.690
What about you, Doctor Ning-nong?

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:05.530
A sheet ghost.

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.670
That is a very cool idea.

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:11.030
Oh, boys.

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:12.120
Whoa.

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:13.810
What are you dressing up as?

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:15.960
I can only guess Jam's costume.

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:17.510
I'm dressing up as a sheet ghost.

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:18.640
Oh, right.

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:20.850
What about you?

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.690
I'm dressing up as a medium.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.930
I'm here to exorcise a certain ghost.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.530
Be careful of exorcising the wrong ghost.

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:32.170
I won't fail. Don't worry.

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:36.530
I'll be on my way, then.

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:38.250
I have to get ready to be the emcee, too.

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:39.220
Alright.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:47.850
Shall we play a game?

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:48.930
Over there.

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:51.410
Let's not. Sarm is arriving soon.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:52.230
Mm.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.550
I can't wait to find out

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:55.810
what ghost Sarm is dressing up as.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.630
Okay, okay.

00:20:58.130 --> 00:20:59.410
I will be back, then.

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:12.620
Let me join you, too.

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:15.840
You know how to use a spirit board?

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:21.940
Thee?

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:25.030
I almost could not recognize you.

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:28.720
Am I so handsome

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:31.330
that you almost did not recognize me?

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:35.430
By the way,

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:38.930
have you ever used a spirit board?

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.340
I have not, actually.

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:43.330
But I want to give it a try.

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:46.220
Let me show you the ropes.

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:48.890
A spirit board...

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:51.150
is like a tool,

00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:53.510
bridging the realm
of the spirits and ours.

00:21:53.940 --> 00:21:55.840
It shows us
what they're trying to communicate.

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:58.410
First, place a finger

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:02.040
on the cup like so.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:06.450
Then, concentrate

00:22:06.480 --> 00:22:07.740
and let the spirit

00:22:08.950 --> 00:22:11.420
communicate with us.

00:22:17.930 --> 00:22:18.820
"D..."

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:23.690
"I..."

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:26.170
"N..."

00:22:26.930 --> 00:22:28.180
"N..."

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:29.580
"E..."

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:30.690
"R..."

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:31.950
"?"

00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:33.860
"Dinner?"

00:22:35.860 --> 00:22:37.000
"W..."

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:38.840
"I..."

00:22:38.860 --> 00:22:40.250
"T-H..."

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:45.220
"M-E-?"

00:22:53.530 --> 00:22:54.700
And...

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:58.710
Where do you want to have dinner?

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:15.690
Please have dinner with me
at my place, Jam.

00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:19.230
And when?

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:26.320
Let's go with...

00:23:39.150 --> 00:23:40.080
Whoa.

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:42.090
Judging by the costume,

00:23:42.110 --> 00:23:44.610
we have to make way for him to make an entrance.

00:23:50.470 --> 00:23:51.940
A lot of you here might be wondering

00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:53.910
what ghost I'm dressing as.

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:55.820
I'm...

00:23:56.050 --> 00:23:57.050
I'm...

00:23:58.630 --> 00:24:00.500
A crab spirit!

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:03.500
A round of applause, please!

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:08.180
Make some noise, and I'll give you a raise!

00:24:11.770 --> 00:24:12.560
First of all,

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:14.520
Happy New Year to everybody here.

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:16.600
Thank you, everyone,

00:24:16.620 --> 00:24:18.750
for taking Adisuan Farm to this point.

00:24:19.010 --> 00:24:20.630
An organization can only grow

00:24:20.720 --> 00:24:21.430
when

00:24:21.450 --> 00:24:23.250
its people grow together.

00:24:26.090 --> 00:24:27.950
I'm losing my voice,
so I'll leave it there.

00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:30.150
I prefer having the results do the talking.

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:31.110
Thank you.

00:24:54.330 --> 00:24:55.330
Hey.

00:24:57.520 --> 00:24:58.520
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Hey.

00:24:59.630 --> 00:25:01.610
I will hit you back.

00:25:09.520 --> 00:25:10.240
Hey.

00:25:11.230 --> 00:25:12.230
Little Jam.

00:25:16.330 --> 00:25:17.330
It's now the new year,

00:25:19.040 --> 00:25:20.320
but I'm still the same old me.

00:25:22.150 --> 00:25:23.640
The same goes for me.

00:25:25.110 --> 00:25:26.550
You're as cute as always.

00:25:29.350 --> 00:25:31.410
And you are as dramatic as usual.

00:25:32.640 --> 00:25:33.450
Whoa.

00:25:36.140 --> 00:25:37.020
It's a new year now.

00:25:37.040 --> 00:25:38.740
Anything you'd like to tell me?

00:25:44.700 --> 00:25:46.790
It is nice knowing you.

00:25:52.520 --> 00:25:54.850
It's nice to know what love is like, too.

00:25:57.940 --> 00:25:59.370
I've got a present for you as well.

00:25:59.680 --> 00:26:01.020
But I can't bring it here tonight.

00:26:02.340 --> 00:26:03.110
Tomorrow,

00:26:03.530 --> 00:26:05.570
you have to go and get it at my place

00:26:06.020 --> 00:26:06.840
by yourself.

00:26:07.830 --> 00:26:08.640
Understand?

00:26:15.060 --> 00:26:16.950
I already have an appointment tomorrow.

00:26:22.120 --> 00:26:22.790
It's fine.

00:26:23.510 --> 00:26:24.620
Late evening will do.

00:26:25.620 --> 00:26:27.020
I can wait, as long as it takes.

00:26:28.740 --> 00:26:29.740
But right now,

00:26:30.590 --> 00:26:32.230
I have a request

00:26:32.640 --> 00:26:33.770
and something to tell you.

00:26:36.750 --> 00:26:37.750
What is it?

00:26:41.930 --> 00:26:42.770
You.

00:26:57.740 --> 00:26:58.740
I...

00:27:02.430 --> 00:27:03.430
You.

00:27:03.640 --> 00:27:04.350
Hm?

00:27:09.350 --> 00:27:10.450
Help me take off this crab suit.

00:27:10.490 --> 00:27:12.570
- Oh, come on.
- Pull the claws.

00:27:12.770 --> 00:27:13.830
Please?

00:27:13.850 --> 00:27:15.080
- Pull the claws.
- Look at me.

00:27:15.100 --> 00:27:15.950
Come on. It won't take long.

00:27:16.300 --> 00:27:17.590
Come on. Help me.

00:27:19.620 --> 00:27:20.330
- I am pulling.
- Hey.

00:27:20.350 --> 00:27:20.970
- Three,
- Be careful.

00:27:20.990 --> 00:27:22.290
two, one.

00:27:23.340 --> 00:27:24.580
Mr. Sarm! Hey!

00:27:24.600 --> 00:27:25.600
Mr. Sarm.

00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:28.110
Grab... Grab onto my arm.

00:27:28.130 --> 00:27:29.240
Sure. I'm alright.

00:27:29.620 --> 00:27:30.620
Thank you.

00:27:31.030 --> 00:27:32.170
Gosh, the crab suit.

00:27:34.240 --> 00:27:35.650
Your hair is a mess.

00:27:36.050 --> 00:27:37.320
- Is it?
- Mm.

00:27:42.910 --> 00:27:43.970
Do I look handsome, though?

00:27:46.630 --> 00:27:47.630
Not sure.

00:27:52.420 --> 00:27:54.530
We had quite a rocky start,

00:27:54.550 --> 00:27:55.230
didn't we?

00:27:59.320 --> 00:28:01.250
But what I want to tell you

00:28:01.270 --> 00:28:02.540
is the truth.

00:28:04.990 --> 00:28:06.420
Listen carefully, okay?

00:28:07.750 --> 00:28:08.850
Don't fall asleep on me.

00:28:16.130 --> 00:28:17.690
You seem serious.

00:28:18.210 --> 00:28:18.930
Very much so.

00:28:19.960 --> 00:28:21.830
No one can be as serious as me.

00:28:24.120 --> 00:28:26.620
Are you leading me here
to pull a prank on me?

00:28:27.390 --> 00:28:28.040
Hey.

00:28:28.580 --> 00:28:30.040
In your eyes,

00:28:30.210 --> 00:28:31.240
what am I like?

00:28:34.140 --> 00:28:34.970
You are slick,

00:28:35.630 --> 00:28:36.570
crazy,

00:28:36.970 --> 00:28:37.970
totally over-the-top,

00:28:38.560 --> 00:28:39.770
overacting,

00:28:40.400 --> 00:28:41.890
and totally unpredictable.

00:28:42.050 --> 00:28:42.940
Oh.

00:28:43.630 --> 00:28:44.500
In truth,

00:28:44.520 --> 00:28:46.360
you did not have to dress up as anything.

00:28:46.380 --> 00:28:47.080
Huh?

00:28:47.350 --> 00:28:49.360
Because you're haunting me
every day like a pervy ghost.

00:28:49.390 --> 00:28:50.750
Oh, Little Jam.

00:28:51.580 --> 00:28:52.330
Ow.

00:28:54.420 --> 00:28:55.840
Does it hurt that much?

00:29:01.970 --> 00:29:03.530
But this man loves you very much.

00:29:09.830 --> 00:29:10.630
I love you.

00:29:12.400 --> 00:29:13.430
I love you, Little Jam.

00:29:17.440 --> 00:29:20.790
♫Time stood still when I met you♫

00:29:20.820 --> 00:29:24.180
♫The way you gazed at me too♫

00:29:24.200 --> 00:29:30.720
♫Couldn't understand what I felt, I had no clue♫

00:29:31.440 --> 00:29:32.730
I love you in every way

00:29:33.130 --> 00:29:34.350
a man is capable of loving someone.

00:29:39.790 --> 00:29:41.240
I've thought it through.

00:29:43.580 --> 00:29:44.690
I don't actually know

00:29:44.710 --> 00:29:46.610
when I started to have this feeling,

00:29:48.880 --> 00:29:51.040
and I couldn't find an answer either.

00:29:57.570 --> 00:29:58.930
By the time I realized it,

00:29:59.540 --> 00:30:00.720
I had already fallen for you.

00:30:04.140 --> 00:30:06.010
Although it seems like
I don't take things seriously,

00:30:06.970 --> 00:30:08.130
let me tell you that

00:30:09.530 --> 00:30:11.530
I'm serious when it comes to loving you.

00:30:15.050 --> 00:30:17.170
But you told me that I was just a burden.

00:30:20.870 --> 00:30:21.940
Can you forgive me, though?

00:30:22.830 --> 00:30:23.640
This man

00:30:23.850 --> 00:30:25.220
was blind to what truly matters.

00:30:26.440 --> 00:30:28.210
You used to call me Snoop.

00:30:28.410 --> 00:30:29.540
Oh.

00:30:31.240 --> 00:30:32.350
Can I beg for your forgiveness?

00:30:33.190 --> 00:30:34.130
I've got flowers

00:30:34.450 --> 00:30:35.570
and incense sticks ready.

00:30:37.470 --> 00:30:39.490
I was once a foul-mouthed person.

00:30:41.820 --> 00:30:43.420
You are allowed to slap me on the lips

00:30:43.880 --> 00:30:45.030
as many times as you'd like.

00:30:50.420 --> 00:30:51.120
There.

00:30:57.780 --> 00:30:59.130
I told you

00:31:00.270 --> 00:31:01.710
not to confess to anyone

00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:04.330
because I wanted to keep your eyes on me.

00:31:10.530 --> 00:31:11.820
I approached you

00:31:12.190 --> 00:31:13.620
as a man,

00:31:15.130 --> 00:31:16.840
not as your boss's younger brother.

00:31:19.950 --> 00:31:22.130
You once only considered me
a Pak Chong branch spouse.

00:31:29.310 --> 00:31:30.530
And I'd like to use this opportunity

00:31:32.730 --> 00:31:34.630
to get an answer from you.

00:31:43.030 --> 00:31:44.340
You once put me at the bottom of the list.

00:31:47.980 --> 00:31:49.720
But can I now be your number one?

00:31:56.450 --> 00:31:57.450
Let's just say...

00:31:59.070 --> 00:32:00.420
If you let me be your number one,

00:32:00.900 --> 00:32:02.220
a kiss means it's a yes.

00:32:28.280 --> 00:32:29.360
Hold me. I'm going to pass out.

00:32:29.380 --> 00:32:30.160
Mr. Sarm!

00:32:30.180 --> 00:32:31.410
Mr. Sarm, Mr. Sarm.

00:32:31.430 --> 00:32:32.220
Mr. Sarm.

00:32:32.740 --> 00:32:34.030
Mr. Sarm...

00:32:35.830 --> 00:32:36.970
Are you okay?

00:32:37.520 --> 00:32:38.610
I am.

00:32:38.630 --> 00:32:39.930
I am very okay.

00:32:40.030 --> 00:32:40.930
Of course, I am.

00:32:41.850 --> 00:32:43.330
Are you hurt?

00:32:44.190 --> 00:32:45.400
I'm very okay. I'm fine.

00:32:46.750 --> 00:32:48.720
I thought something happened to you.

00:32:49.520 --> 00:32:50.720
It was nothing.

00:32:56.290 --> 00:32:57.130
Let's go home.

00:33:00.250 --> 00:33:01.250
Right.

00:33:02.550 --> 00:33:09.090
♫I'll stay right here by your side, always♫

00:33:09.320 --> 00:33:10.450
Can I have another kiss?

00:33:11.970 --> 00:33:13.630
You had enough.

00:33:16.560 --> 00:33:17.230
Gosh.

00:33:24.310 --> 00:33:25.820
Gosh, come on.

00:33:26.930 --> 00:33:27.930
"I love you, Little Jam."

00:33:29.070 --> 00:33:30.170
"I love you, Little Jam."

00:33:31.240 --> 00:33:32.240
"I love you, Little Jam."

00:33:33.450 --> 00:33:34.620
"I love you, Little Jam."

00:33:35.630 --> 00:33:36.920
"I love you, Little Jam."

00:33:37.660 --> 00:33:40.630
His confession still lingers in my mind.

00:33:41.620 --> 00:33:43.920
But tonight, I have a mission to take care of.

00:33:45.020 --> 00:33:47.540
How will the results turn out, I wonder?

00:33:57.930 --> 00:33:59.240
Hello, Song.

00:34:01.020 --> 00:34:02.200
Hi there, Jam.

00:34:02.620 --> 00:34:03.340
Take a seat.

00:34:03.660 --> 00:34:04.640
Thank you.

00:34:09.199 --> 00:34:10.650
Where are you off to
at such an early hour?

00:34:10.719 --> 00:34:12.130
Isn't today everybody's day off?

00:34:12.230 --> 00:34:13.320
It is.

00:34:13.730 --> 00:34:15.330
I am here to get some coffee.

00:34:17.389 --> 00:34:18.889
Where are you going?

00:34:19.820 --> 00:34:21.400
I was just done with my shift.

00:34:21.500 --> 00:34:23.230
I am about to go and rest up for a bit.

00:34:23.409 --> 00:34:24.750
I am terribly sleepy right now.

00:34:26.870 --> 00:34:27.920
Oh, tonight,

00:34:27.949 --> 00:34:30.050
there's dinner at the main house.

00:34:30.380 --> 00:34:32.630
Sib and PiMai are going there.

00:34:33.090 --> 00:34:35.320
Jam... Are you interested in being there?

00:34:38.030 --> 00:34:40.050
I am already occupied this evening.

00:34:41.610 --> 00:34:42.610
Is that so?

00:34:43.449 --> 00:34:44.929
That's a shame, really.

00:34:45.219 --> 00:34:45.820
And...

00:34:46.590 --> 00:34:48.130
Where are you off to this evening?

00:34:50.280 --> 00:34:51.550
Thee's place.

00:34:52.540 --> 00:34:54.230
Lately, we have been
working together a lot.

00:34:56.340 --> 00:34:57.740
Uh-huh, Thee's place.

00:35:00.030 --> 00:35:00.630
Oh.

00:35:00.950 --> 00:35:02.230
Last night,

00:35:02.250 --> 00:35:03.580
there was a party, wasn't there?

00:35:03.690 --> 00:35:05.970
I heard that the theme
was ghost-related, right?

00:35:06.220 --> 00:35:06.940
Did you have fun?

00:35:07.200 --> 00:35:09.890
You must've looked cute
in your costume.

00:35:12.570 --> 00:35:13.940
It was pretty fun.

00:35:15.330 --> 00:35:16.410
"I love you, Little Jam."

00:35:17.330 --> 00:35:18.640
"I love you, Little Jam."

00:35:19.530 --> 00:35:20.570
"I love you, Little Jam."

00:35:22.270 --> 00:35:22.940
So...

00:35:24.320 --> 00:35:25.430
Sarm...

00:35:25.530 --> 00:35:27.420
confessed his love to you, didn't he?

00:35:28.640 --> 00:35:29.970
You knew?

00:35:32.140 --> 00:35:33.520
Of course, I knew.

00:35:33.990 --> 00:35:36.640
Sarm and I are twins, remember?

00:35:37.240 --> 00:35:39.120
We keep no secrets from each other.

00:35:44.300 --> 00:35:45.930
With that, I had the answer.

00:35:46.200 --> 00:35:47.330
I saw right through you.

00:35:48.750 --> 00:35:49.520
And...

00:35:50.030 --> 00:35:52.630
What did you say?

00:35:54.030 --> 00:35:55.120
Am I close to having...

00:35:55.430 --> 00:35:57.030
a brother-in-law?

00:35:59.830 --> 00:36:01.630
I did not say anything.

00:36:03.230 --> 00:36:04.530
I think

00:36:05.530 --> 00:36:06.940
you should just say yes.

00:36:08.330 --> 00:36:10.130
Thinking about it
already gives me a headache.

00:36:12.030 --> 00:36:13.330
You're right.

00:36:20.250 --> 00:36:21.730
Excuse me.

00:36:24.130 --> 00:36:26.330
Mr. Sarm, would you like to have lunch right now?

00:36:27.640 --> 00:36:28.940
I'm good, Aunt.

00:36:29.650 --> 00:36:30.450
I...

00:36:31.250 --> 00:36:32.330
It's too much to eat anything.

00:36:32.630 --> 00:36:33.810
Are you feeling unwell?

00:36:33.910 --> 00:36:35.170
Are you having a stomachache?

00:36:35.240 --> 00:36:36.520
Do you want me to call a doctor?

00:36:38.430 --> 00:36:39.430
It's okay.

00:36:39.770 --> 00:36:40.630
I...

00:36:43.720 --> 00:36:46.090
I'm extremely fulfilled.

00:36:46.910 --> 00:36:48.650
I can just live like this for years

00:36:48.760 --> 00:36:49.970
without eating anything.

00:36:50.130 --> 00:36:52.020
I'm over the moon right now.

00:36:55.340 --> 00:36:56.650
It's like I'm mentally fulfilled.

00:36:57.320 --> 00:36:58.510
Hunger means nothing.

00:36:58.530 --> 00:36:59.820
I'm overjoyed.

00:36:59.840 --> 00:37:00.810
I'll skip lunch.

00:37:01.310 --> 00:37:02.370
Right...

00:37:04.920 --> 00:37:07.290
♫Can I give a cutie like you a kiss?♫

00:37:07.310 --> 00:37:09.050
♫Can I give you one more kiss?♫

00:37:09.090 --> 00:37:11.080
♫You♫

00:37:11.100 --> 00:37:12.580
♫Just a bit more♫

00:37:12.600 --> 00:37:14.310
♫Can I kiss you one more time?♫

00:37:14.330 --> 00:37:16.080
♫Can I give you one more kiss?♫

00:37:16.100 --> 00:37:18.210
♫I'm not gonna lie♫

00:37:18.230 --> 00:37:21.510
♫If I can't kiss you now, I'd lose my mind♫

00:37:25.320 --> 00:37:28.580
♫If I can't kiss you now, I'd lose my mind♫

00:37:37.330 --> 00:37:38.930
Good evening, Thee.

00:37:39.510 --> 00:37:40.380
Hi.

00:37:40.740 --> 00:37:42.240
You look extremely lovely this evening.

00:37:43.430 --> 00:37:44.120
No...

00:37:45.130 --> 00:37:46.850
You look this lovely every day.

00:37:49.340 --> 00:37:50.920
You are also looking good.

00:37:54.040 --> 00:37:54.920
Thank you.

00:37:55.270 --> 00:37:56.290
Shall we get going, then?

00:37:56.630 --> 00:37:57.410
Sure.

00:37:58.130 --> 00:37:59.000
This way.

00:37:59.020 --> 00:38:00.020
Right.

00:38:22.730 --> 00:38:23.440
This way.

00:38:24.030 --> 00:38:24.840
Alright.

00:38:58.140 --> 00:38:59.140
Please take a seat.

00:39:00.750 --> 00:39:01.750
Thank you.

00:39:02.910 --> 00:39:03.910
Mm...

00:39:04.160 --> 00:39:06.010
I didn't actually know...

00:39:06.030 --> 00:39:07.430
what kind of food you prefer,

00:39:08.230 --> 00:39:09.630
so I made you steak.

00:39:11.760 --> 00:39:13.210
Looks very appetizing.

00:39:16.750 --> 00:39:18.360
I also...

00:39:19.730 --> 00:39:21.720
I do kind of know how to cook.

00:39:22.930 --> 00:39:26.840
I poured my heart and soul into it.

00:39:29.240 --> 00:39:31.720
I wanted you to give it a try.

00:39:38.230 --> 00:39:39.850
Well...

00:39:42.040 --> 00:39:44.830
Can I post it on my IG Stories?

00:39:46.730 --> 00:39:48.530
Would you mind, Thee?

00:39:49.830 --> 00:39:50.550
No problem.

00:39:52.630 --> 00:39:53.630
Alright.

00:40:13.050 --> 00:40:14.050
Mm...

00:40:17.390 --> 00:40:19.420
Would you like to film
some IG Stories with me?

00:40:28.030 --> 00:40:29.230
Would it be a good idea?

00:40:30.630 --> 00:40:32.830
If your partner got it all wrong,

00:40:34.240 --> 00:40:35.750
I am not to blame...

00:40:38.130 --> 00:40:39.130
Mm...

00:40:42.040 --> 00:40:44.340
Let me tell you something.

00:40:44.650 --> 00:40:45.650
Well...

00:40:47.940 --> 00:40:49.150
I'm single.

00:40:51.120 --> 00:40:52.410
And...

00:40:53.820 --> 00:40:55.830
I don't want to be single anymore.

00:41:00.940 --> 00:41:02.730
From here,

00:41:02.750 --> 00:41:04.330
the view is rather beautiful.

00:41:12.580 --> 00:41:13.580
It is, isn't it?

00:41:15.070 --> 00:41:16.660
Whenever I'm stressed out,

00:41:16.680 --> 00:41:18.460
I'd just sit down and enjoy the view.

00:41:20.230 --> 00:41:23.620
Seeing something
I created with my own hands makes me...

00:41:24.510 --> 00:41:27.740
feel somewhat proud of myself.

00:41:29.950 --> 00:41:30.980
As for me,

00:41:31.000 --> 00:41:33.430
all I've been doing is working,

00:41:33.640 --> 00:41:35.610
constantly doing this and that.

00:41:35.630 --> 00:41:36.840
I haven't caught a break at all.

00:41:46.690 --> 00:41:49.930
That is why Adisuan Farm has grown this much.

00:41:53.480 --> 00:41:54.440
Right, Jam?

00:41:56.550 --> 00:41:57.730
Let me tell you this.

00:41:58.370 --> 00:42:00.400
I've done a lot for this empire,

00:42:00.840 --> 00:42:01.840
and...

00:42:02.130 --> 00:42:05.040
I'm Uncle Decha's only grandson.

00:42:06.430 --> 00:42:08.630
So I think...

00:42:09.780 --> 00:42:12.220
Adisuan Farm
should belong to me, shouldn't it?

00:42:16.730 --> 00:42:17.730
But...

00:42:19.140 --> 00:42:21.420
Uncle Decha has heirs, does he not?

00:42:25.220 --> 00:42:26.340
The brats at the main house?

00:42:27.490 --> 00:42:28.530
Know this.

00:42:28.990 --> 00:42:31.110
They're all his problematic children,

00:42:32.940 --> 00:42:34.130
especially Sarm.

00:42:35.570 --> 00:42:36.230
That brat

00:42:36.250 --> 00:42:37.950
is always causing trouble for people

00:42:38.140 --> 00:42:40.050
whenever he does something.

00:42:40.430 --> 00:42:41.730
Without me,

00:42:42.630 --> 00:42:45.010
no one else could've taken
Adisuan Farm this far.

00:42:46.130 --> 00:42:47.510
No wonder

00:42:49.240 --> 00:42:52.640
someone was hunting him down

00:42:53.140 --> 00:42:55.500
when I was tasked with bringing
Mr. Sarm back from Ko Pha-ngan.

00:42:55.830 --> 00:42:59.160
It's because
he always causes trouble for others.

00:43:02.120 --> 00:43:03.730
He is the worst.

00:43:13.160 --> 00:43:15.420
By the way...

00:43:17.430 --> 00:43:19.180
Were you involved, too, Jam?

00:43:32.350 --> 00:43:33.310
Is it uncomfortable?

00:43:35.310 --> 00:43:36.310
Not at all, I guess?

00:43:40.540 --> 00:43:41.540
Want to join us?

00:43:42.340 --> 00:43:43.610
Come. It'll be nice and cozy.

00:43:43.850 --> 00:43:44.480
PiMai, come on.

00:43:44.500 --> 00:43:45.710
There's still room for me?

00:43:45.730 --> 00:43:47.030
It's fine. Come on.

00:43:49.310 --> 00:43:50.520
Hey, wait, kiddo.

00:43:50.810 --> 00:43:51.810
You shouldn't.

00:43:52.230 --> 00:43:53.670
It's already too hard to breathe.

00:43:55.140 --> 00:43:55.830
Okay.

00:43:55.850 --> 00:43:57.160
And you shouldn't have said that.

00:43:57.430 --> 00:43:58.760
Dad!

00:43:58.810 --> 00:43:59.580
It's fine for you two to have some space.

00:43:59.600 --> 00:44:00.940
There's still a lot more room left.

00:44:02.650 --> 00:44:03.440
Sib,

00:44:03.740 --> 00:44:04.740
do you want to have baos with me?

00:44:06.530 --> 00:44:07.820
He's probably sick of eating them.

00:44:09.190 --> 00:44:11.450
You should find something
to stuff your mouth with, Sarm.

00:44:12.070 --> 00:44:12.830
Why?

00:44:13.320 --> 00:44:14.210
Worried about me?

00:44:14.260 --> 00:44:15.200
You're worried I'd get hungry?

00:44:15.260 --> 00:44:16.440
No, not at all.

00:44:16.460 --> 00:44:17.590
Go get something to eat,

00:44:17.610 --> 00:44:18.680
so you'll stop talking.

00:44:18.700 --> 00:44:20.100
Is it wrong that I'm talking?

00:44:20.210 --> 00:44:20.890
Of course not,

00:44:20.910 --> 00:44:21.800
but it's annoying.

00:44:21.820 --> 00:44:22.600
- Sarm.
- It's not.

00:44:22.620 --> 00:44:23.840
- Dad loves my voice.
- What do you think, Dad?

00:44:23.860 --> 00:44:24.570
Shut it.

00:44:24.590 --> 00:44:25.490
- I'm talking to Dad here.
- Hey, that's enough.

00:44:25.510 --> 00:44:27.420
Enough already, you two.

00:44:27.510 --> 00:44:28.560
Take a breather.

00:44:28.760 --> 00:44:29.780
Stop it.

00:44:29.800 --> 00:44:30.540
Listen.

00:44:31.030 --> 00:44:33.170
Aren't you a bit too obsessed
with your phone, huh?

00:44:33.190 --> 00:44:34.250
I'm not.

00:44:35.900 --> 00:44:36.960
But I'm obsessed with...

00:44:37.010 --> 00:44:38.220
someone I chat with on my phone.

00:44:42.880 --> 00:44:43.610
Song.

00:44:43.630 --> 00:44:44.240
Huh?

00:44:44.260 --> 00:44:45.810
After we're done here,

00:44:46.470 --> 00:44:48.080
help me wrap a present at the quarters.

00:44:48.100 --> 00:44:49.160
- Wrap a present?
- Yeah.

00:44:49.180 --> 00:44:49.920
What present?

00:44:49.940 --> 00:44:50.940
How big can it be?

00:44:51.830 --> 00:44:53.160
Well, you have to wrap me.

00:44:53.180 --> 00:44:53.570
Huh?

00:44:53.590 --> 00:44:54.520
Put a ribbon on me, too.

00:44:55.490 --> 00:44:56.350
You're nuts.

00:44:56.490 --> 00:44:57.370
What are you doing this for?

00:44:57.540 --> 00:44:58.140
What?

00:44:58.880 --> 00:45:01.250
I want to be Jam's present.

00:45:02.040 --> 00:45:02.820
Also...

00:45:03.330 --> 00:45:04.930
I want to make it official, too.

00:45:04.950 --> 00:45:05.830
Are you serious?

00:45:06.650 --> 00:45:07.440
This is cringe.

00:45:09.470 --> 00:45:10.930
Sib, are you alright?

00:45:12.590 --> 00:45:14.130
I haven't been able to reach Jam,

00:45:14.830 --> 00:45:15.830
which is unusual.

00:45:16.380 --> 00:45:17.520
What time is it?

00:45:20.440 --> 00:45:21.230
It's almost 8 P.M.

00:45:23.250 --> 00:45:24.160
Quit it while you can,

00:45:24.180 --> 00:45:25.910
asking someone to work overtime.

00:45:25.930 --> 00:45:27.210
Humans aren't robots.

00:45:27.320 --> 00:45:28.730
Little Jam is this tiny.

00:45:30.730 --> 00:45:32.240
"Little Jam," you said?

00:45:32.490 --> 00:45:33.490
Let me tell you something.

00:45:33.510 --> 00:45:34.850
I always pay him for the overtime.

00:45:35.690 --> 00:45:36.730
I know.

00:45:40.510 --> 00:45:41.920
I think...

00:45:42.540 --> 00:45:44.420
You're a bit out of the loop, Sib.

00:45:45.710 --> 00:45:46.790
What am I missing?

00:45:47.530 --> 00:45:48.120
Yeah.

00:45:48.370 --> 00:45:49.520
I also want to say that

00:45:49.540 --> 00:45:50.820
Jam will be with me tonight.

00:45:51.970 --> 00:45:53.040
And let me tell you this.

00:45:53.340 --> 00:45:54.550
If you need something from him,

00:45:54.740 --> 00:45:55.930
discuss it with him later.

00:45:56.530 --> 00:45:57.320
You're right.

00:45:57.540 --> 00:46:00.240
Sib always overworks Mr. Jam.

00:46:01.310 --> 00:46:03.140
- Right, PiMai?
- Goodness me...

00:46:03.230 --> 00:46:03.910
I

00:46:03.930 --> 00:46:05.610
will have Jam stay here.

00:46:05.630 --> 00:46:06.930
I won't give him back either.

00:46:07.840 --> 00:46:08.600
- How's that sound?
- PiMai!

00:46:08.720 --> 00:46:09.340
Sounds good.

00:46:09.360 --> 00:46:10.210
Right?

00:46:10.680 --> 00:46:11.610
PiMai.

00:46:14.840 --> 00:46:15.840
Take that.

00:46:22.410 --> 00:46:23.410
Correct.

00:46:24.040 --> 00:46:27.330
I got caught up
in Mr. Sarm's business as well.

00:46:28.030 --> 00:46:31.490
At first, we ran
and ended up at a fishing village.

00:46:32.350 --> 00:46:35.650
But eventually, the thugs found us.

00:46:36.130 --> 00:46:38.020
Now that you know,

00:46:38.660 --> 00:46:40.030
please keep this a secret.

00:46:50.250 --> 00:46:51.250
Of course.

00:46:52.930 --> 00:46:54.830
Uh, by the way...

00:46:55.950 --> 00:46:57.230
What's next?

00:47:02.290 --> 00:47:05.240
When they found us for the second time,

00:47:08.640 --> 00:47:11.050
we would have escaped if we had tried,

00:47:12.230 --> 00:47:13.640
but Mr. Sarm

00:47:13.820 --> 00:47:15.130
did not take the situation seriously,

00:47:15.420 --> 00:47:18.170
so they caught us and put us on their boat.

00:47:19.610 --> 00:47:21.040
As I've said, Jam.

00:47:22.640 --> 00:47:24.030
Sarm is incompetent.

00:47:25.030 --> 00:47:28.050
He couldn't even handle
a handful of thugs himself.

00:47:29.470 --> 00:47:31.470
On top of that, the boat they were using

00:47:31.640 --> 00:47:32.830
was so old that

00:47:33.930 --> 00:47:36.230
if he chose to make an escape,

00:47:36.850 --> 00:47:38.120
he would've gotten away.

00:47:39.430 --> 00:47:41.420
A handful of men.

00:47:42.030 --> 00:47:43.930
An old boat.

00:47:46.730 --> 00:47:48.170
Was that what you said, Thee?

00:47:48.350 --> 00:47:49.290
You heard me.

00:47:50.940 --> 00:47:53.690
Though there were only a few of them,

00:47:55.240 --> 00:47:56.730
they all looked like badasses.

00:47:59.930 --> 00:48:02.810
If the underlings were already that cool,

00:48:06.950 --> 00:48:09.440
I wonder how cool the boss would be.

00:48:12.840 --> 00:48:15.970
I think the boss must look like
the main character from Prison Break.

00:48:17.440 --> 00:48:18.930
He is so my type.

00:48:23.350 --> 00:48:24.730
"Your type," you said?

00:48:25.430 --> 00:48:26.430
Yes.

00:48:28.520 --> 00:48:29.780
Take a seat.

00:48:30.350 --> 00:48:31.430
Have a seat.

00:48:33.300 --> 00:48:34.240
Mm...

00:48:36.130 --> 00:48:36.760
Jam.

00:48:37.930 --> 00:48:40.120
I think...

00:48:42.780 --> 00:48:44.730
I've got something

00:48:45.930 --> 00:48:47.220
to tell you.

00:48:48.030 --> 00:48:49.330
It's a secret, too.

00:48:51.940 --> 00:48:53.140
Listen up.

00:48:56.330 --> 00:48:57.330
It was me

00:48:59.890 --> 00:49:02.030
who sent those men to get rid of Sarm

00:49:03.730 --> 00:49:05.420
once and for all.

00:49:08.660 --> 00:49:11.850
Sarm doesn't deserve
to rule the Adisuan empire.

00:49:13.450 --> 00:49:14.970
Don't you agree?

00:49:22.040 --> 00:49:24.930
You truly deserve to rule Adisuan Farm.

00:49:30.230 --> 00:49:31.620
By the way...

00:49:35.430 --> 00:49:37.030
I'm this talented,

00:49:38.950 --> 00:49:40.640
and you're not interested in me?

00:49:44.240 --> 00:49:47.240
What do you mean by that, Thee?

00:49:49.240 --> 00:49:51.540
What I'm saying is this...

00:49:54.940 --> 00:49:56.530
I'm interested in you.

00:49:58.330 --> 00:49:59.410
I like you.

00:50:01.130 --> 00:50:04.120
Do you know that I've been wanting to
get to know you since I first saw you,

00:50:04.150 --> 00:50:05.150
hm?

00:50:06.630 --> 00:50:07.630
And aside from that...

00:50:10.630 --> 00:50:13.020
What is your type, Jam?

00:50:18.590 --> 00:50:20.440
I have no preferences.

00:50:21.630 --> 00:50:23.320
I love whoever I feel like loving.

00:50:23.910 --> 00:50:24.540
Mm.

00:50:24.580 --> 00:50:26.150
Come on, Jam.

00:50:27.190 --> 00:50:28.450
Mm...

00:50:28.470 --> 00:50:30.820
Just tell me. I'm curious to find out.

00:50:32.980 --> 00:50:35.530
I love the type of person who is cheerful

00:50:37.230 --> 00:50:39.620
and knows when to have fun

00:50:42.230 --> 00:50:44.830
and be serious.

00:50:47.940 --> 00:50:48.940
You hit the nail on the head.

00:50:50.320 --> 00:50:51.870
The type of person you just described,

00:50:51.900 --> 00:50:52.830
I think...

00:50:54.470 --> 00:50:55.730
it's basically me.

00:50:56.820 --> 00:50:57.820
Wouldn't you agree?

00:50:58.930 --> 00:50:59.730
Oh...

00:51:14.630 --> 00:51:15.730
What does this mean?

00:51:24.860 --> 00:51:26.620
What does this mean,

00:51:27.120 --> 00:51:27.820
hm?

00:51:28.770 --> 00:51:29.890
No answer?!

00:51:30.540 --> 00:51:31.540
Come here!

00:51:32.010 --> 00:51:33.000
Are you going to spit it out,

00:51:33.040 --> 00:51:33.760
huh?

00:51:37.690 --> 00:51:39.010
I'm asking you what the fuck that means.

00:51:48.430 --> 00:51:49.170
Come here.

00:51:51.230 --> 00:51:52.600
What the fuck is this shit, huh?!

00:51:54.490 --> 00:51:55.960
How dare you?!

00:51:56.390 --> 00:51:58.020
Think you can fool me, huh?!

00:52:01.170 --> 00:52:02.830
I adored you, Jam.

00:52:03.650 --> 00:52:06.330
Taking my phone from me changes nothing.

00:52:06.840 --> 00:52:09.130
I have already made hundreds of copies
of the audio files.

00:52:10.530 --> 00:52:13.110
If I disappear for more than two hours,

00:52:15.330 --> 00:52:18.340
a voice message will be sent to
Mr. Sib automatically.

00:52:19.740 --> 00:52:21.970
You are doomed either way.

00:52:23.830 --> 00:52:25.030
Your best bet...

00:52:26.430 --> 00:52:28.340
is to confess your crime.

00:52:29.320 --> 00:52:30.930
You still have time.

00:52:35.480 --> 00:52:36.920
Confess my crime?

00:52:47.980 --> 00:52:49.720
You want me to confess?!

00:52:54.520 --> 00:52:55.820
If you...

00:52:56.440 --> 00:52:58.420
If you can't make it out of this place,

00:52:59.540 --> 00:53:02.050
no one will ever know

00:53:02.230 --> 00:53:04.030
what we discussed here.

00:53:05.940 --> 00:53:08.710
About you sending men
to get rid of Mr. Sarm,

00:53:10.350 --> 00:53:12.250
though Mr. Sarm knew nothing,

00:53:14.230 --> 00:53:15.570
Mr. Sib knew all about it.

00:53:16.820 --> 00:53:18.140
All that he needs is evidence.

00:53:19.430 --> 00:53:20.430
Evidence?

00:53:23.740 --> 00:53:24.820
You mean this?

00:53:25.040 --> 00:53:25.830
Sheesh.

00:53:29.540 --> 00:53:31.130
That is no toy.

00:53:32.830 --> 00:53:34.430
You will pay for it,

00:53:37.210 --> 00:53:39.830
including for hurting me.

00:53:41.870 --> 00:53:43.810
I will not let this slide.

00:53:45.830 --> 00:53:47.690
I will have my revenge.

00:53:52.320 --> 00:53:53.930
You want to have your revenge?!

00:53:55.550 --> 00:53:57.890
Before you can do that,

00:53:58.720 --> 00:54:01.440
how about you make sure
you can survive this night,

00:54:02.220 --> 00:54:03.050
huh?

00:54:03.740 --> 00:54:06.120
What should I do with you, Jam?

00:54:08.730 --> 00:54:09.520
Oh.

00:54:10.540 --> 00:54:11.540
Well...

00:54:11.940 --> 00:54:13.030
How about this?

00:54:15.620 --> 00:54:17.890
I will bring your laptop here,

00:54:18.480 --> 00:54:21.110
and you have to get rid of the audio files.

00:54:21.130 --> 00:54:22.330
Every single one of them.

00:54:23.060 --> 00:54:24.060
Then,

00:54:25.570 --> 00:54:27.220
I'll let you go.

00:54:29.240 --> 00:54:31.210
But after that,

00:54:32.720 --> 00:54:34.690
you have to behave.

00:54:36.200 --> 00:54:37.950
Don't do anything stupid.

00:54:40.020 --> 00:54:41.330
You know that

00:54:42.500 --> 00:54:44.130
you can't escape from me, don't you?

00:54:47.420 --> 00:54:49.840
With what you have done to me,

00:54:53.330 --> 00:54:55.620
do you think I can?

00:54:58.030 --> 00:54:59.610
It's nice that you know that.

00:55:07.250 --> 00:55:08.250
- Ow!
- Hey!

00:55:10.340 --> 00:55:11.300
Why are you so hard to get,

00:55:11.330 --> 00:55:11.930
huh?!

00:55:14.640 --> 00:55:15.720
Know this!

00:55:17.040 --> 00:55:18.040
Don't.

00:55:21.340 --> 00:55:22.340
Don't.

00:55:23.150 --> 00:55:25.120
Don't do anything stupid,

00:55:26.080 --> 00:55:27.010
okay?

00:55:32.970 --> 00:55:34.810
- Ah!
- Whoa!

00:55:35.430 --> 00:55:36.810
The gunshot
was from the very end of the farm.

00:55:37.160 --> 00:55:38.250
Maybe it came from Thee's place.

00:55:38.830 --> 00:55:40.020
Thee's... Thee's place?

00:55:40.040 --> 00:55:40.530
Mm.

00:55:40.560 --> 00:55:41.730
This means that

00:55:41.750 --> 00:55:43.450
Jam is in danger.

00:55:43.470 --> 00:55:43.910
Huh?!

00:55:43.930 --> 00:55:44.930
- What do you mean?
- What?

00:55:44.960 --> 00:55:45.860
This morning,

00:55:45.880 --> 00:55:46.770
I met Jam,

00:55:46.790 --> 00:55:47.820
and he told me that

00:55:47.840 --> 00:55:49.440
he's meeting Thee at his place tonight.

00:55:50.570 --> 00:55:51.940
Song, contact the doctors.

00:55:51.960 --> 00:55:52.700
Sarm.

00:55:52.720 --> 00:55:54.560
Sib, if you wouldn't mind,

00:55:54.580 --> 00:55:55.480
please go to my place.

00:55:55.500 --> 00:55:56.790
If Jam comes back and doesn't see me,

00:55:56.810 --> 00:55:57.650
at least he'll see you there.

00:56:00.540 --> 00:56:01.390
Come on!

00:56:02.740 --> 00:56:03.740
Ow...

00:56:05.290 --> 00:56:06.030
Ow...

00:56:10.030 --> 00:56:11.420
Wait here.

00:56:12.530 --> 00:56:13.530
I'll be right back.

00:56:44.210 --> 00:56:45.520
Jam! Jam!

00:56:45.940 --> 00:56:46.550
Jam.

00:56:47.140 --> 00:56:48.340
Mr. Sarm, you must listen to me.

00:56:49.430 --> 00:56:52.810
I now know who sent those men
to hunt you down back at Ko Pha-ngan.

00:56:53.810 --> 00:56:54.940
It was Mr. Thee.

00:56:55.490 --> 00:56:57.130
He was behind it all.

00:56:57.640 --> 00:56:59.040
I have the evidence.

00:56:59.420 --> 00:57:00.630
I have the audio recording.

00:57:02.460 --> 00:57:04.830
But he threw my phone and broke it.

00:57:06.380 --> 00:57:07.840
But do not worry.

00:57:08.240 --> 00:57:10.140
I have sent the recording to Mr. Sib.

00:57:12.310 --> 00:57:13.850
You do not have to worry about it now.

00:57:17.840 --> 00:57:18.840
That bastard did this to you?

00:57:23.430 --> 00:57:24.360
Call Sib.

00:57:24.650 --> 00:57:25.650
He'll take you to the doctor.

00:57:26.050 --> 00:57:26.720
Can you still drive?

00:57:26.740 --> 00:57:27.810
Where are you going?

00:57:28.090 --> 00:57:29.050
I'll be right back.

00:57:31.750 --> 00:57:33.040
Mr. Sarm.

00:57:34.540 --> 00:57:35.540
Mr. Sarm!

00:57:36.820 --> 00:57:38.290
Mr. Sarm!

00:57:45.220 --> 00:57:45.630
Hey!

00:57:45.650 --> 00:57:46.160
I was just...

00:57:46.180 --> 00:57:47.400
Asshole!

00:57:51.530 --> 00:57:53.820
